92186329483 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186329118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329483 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329483 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329483 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186328180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329483 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "abc88ab4-86f2-5a4b-8e4f-88060e4ebc03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329660 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329660 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42502" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329660 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329660 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=2.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329660 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2475d475-902a-59fd-8c1f-992bd3a67e4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329660 #edb/ref 1074 "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{3}{2}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329708 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186329300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329708 #edb/ref 1069 "q-43081" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329708 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329708 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $A$ and $B$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(A)=-108$, find $det(B).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186329708 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47c11704-21a6-552f-bee3-3f4e3309d6d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186329708 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $B$ can be obtained from $A$ by multiplying the $2$nd row by $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nSo, the determinant is multiplied by $-\\frac{1}{2}$ as well.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-108) \\\\  & =54.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339153 #edb/ref 1080 "13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339153 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339153 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03d100ee-988b-5858-8aa5-ab77698f84d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339339 #edb/ref 1080 "-36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339339 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339339 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17922ecf-87f8-5af9-872a-3d5dc6da26af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339357 #edb/ref 1080 "-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339357 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339357 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "19fbca7f-f430-54fe-98d9-b7f7f315925a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339679 #edb/ref 1080 "-13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339679 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339679 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3da4d93c-6b55-5cee-b637-5ba85976a8bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339686 #edb/ref 1080 "-243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339686 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339686 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3e3f2587-b4ad-5bf0-81b7-1df62ffb7a09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339736 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339736 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339736 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "44b41ca8-7df3-5293-a744-43b0e1afa203" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340110 #edb/ref 1080 "40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340110 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340110 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6eaa8f7b-0624-52d4-867d-8074d8a609c5" #edb/r