7] [17592186341773 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ded707a6-03c1-52cc-8868-8933afddd3df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341848 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341848 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72716" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341848 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341848 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $X$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(X)=-13.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{2}$ (switching the second and the fifth rows). What is the value of $det(Y)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341848 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e679b14-a7d9-5eaa-ba4a-ea8d4a8b2fc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341848 #edb/ref 1074 "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(-13) \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341851 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341851 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341851 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341851 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-64.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{5}{8}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341851 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2858ce5b-8e2a-5132-aac3-acedb511e7f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341851 #edb/ref 1074 "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{5}{8}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =\\frac{5}{8}det(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-64) \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378658 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378658 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378