045417] [17592186383181 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $C$ is a $9\\times 9$ matrix and $det(C)=-93.$ The matrix $D$ is obtained from $C$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{9}:=-\\frac{5}{31}{R}_{9}.$ What is the value of $det(D)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383181 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ecc2dd8-459c-57bc-a2ce-f5ea52a64697" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383181 #edb/ref 1074 "The row operation applied to $C$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{5}{31}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-\\frac{5}{31}det(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{31}\\cdot (-93) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186383184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383182 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b4fa9a35-54b0-560c-ba75-0ddbfc721ada" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383183 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383183 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383183 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b0b05031-46de-5688-a455-e96dab770004" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383184 #edb/ref 1080 "15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383184 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383184 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "24272a72-651d-5527-872e-1bbd054048eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383185 #edb/ref 1080 "18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383185 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383185 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "86182598-d0ed-54fc-bb0e-ad0d9d3072ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383186 #edb/ref 1080 "-21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383186 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383186 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a88007ae-aa92-54fe-8b6f-a828e87edeab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383187 #edb/ref 1080 "-12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383187 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383187 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "54736168-6ad1-5a53-a707-3dd8eb0d5dca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186383196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383195 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130737" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383195 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383195 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $C$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(C)=-5.$ What is the value of $det(-2C)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a5f04aa-dd8a-5322-9e5d-a0849f397bd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383195 #edb/ref 1074 "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-2$ and $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-2C) & =(-2)^{4}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383196 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383196 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383196 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383196 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383196 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186383201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186383196 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #e